<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacopo I da Carrara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1324">1324</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacopo I da <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrara">Carrara</a> was a Paduan nobleman elected lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> in 1318, when the commune sought a strong leader against Cangrande della Scala of Verona. His election founded the rule of the Carrara family, which lasted with interruptions until 1405. He died in 1324, and Padua fell to Verona four years later.</p></div>
